<div class="landing landing-home">
  <div class="home-top">
    <.marketing_nav current_user={assigns[:current_user]} active={:pricing} />

    <section class="home-hero home-hero-compact">
      <div class="home-wrap">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h1>Free to publish. Paid when you want a domain of your own.</h1>
        <p class="home-lede">
          Every site starts free and stays free. There is no trial and nothing expires.
          A license is per site, so you only pay for the ones that need a custom domain
          or a team behind them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="plans-title">
    <div class="home-wrap">
      <h2 id="plans-title">Two plans, per site</h2>

      <div class="price-plans">
        <article class="price-plan">
          <h3>Free</h3>
          <p class="price-amount">{@free_price}<span>forever</span></p>
          <p class="price-sub">Everything you need to write and publish.</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Unlimited posts and pages</li>
            <li>Write in Markdown or HTML</li>
            <li>Themes from the marketplace, or upload your own</li>
            <li>A <code>yoursite.masthead.site</code> address</li>
            <li>Automatic HTTPS</li>
            <li>Image and file uploads</li>
            <li>Tags and drafts</li>
            <li>Import an existing Hugo site</li>
          </ul>

          <.link
            :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
            navigate={~p"/signup"}
            class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg price-action"
          >
            Create your site
          </.link>
          <.link
            :if={assigns[:current_user]}
            navigate={~p"/sites"}
            class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg price-action"
          >
            Open dashboard
          </.link>
        </article>

        <article class="price-plan price-plan-paid">
          <h3>
            Paid <span :if={@saving} class="price-saving">Save {@saving} a year</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="price-amount">{@monthly_price}<span>per month</span></p>
          <p class="price-sub">or {@yearly_price} billed yearly. Cancel any time.</p>

          <ul>
            <li class="price-list-head">Everything in Free, plus:</li>
            <li>Your own custom domain, apex or subdomain</li>
            <li>TLS certificates provisioned automatically</li>
            <li>Invite collaborators to the site</li>
            <li>Visitor statistics, without cookies or a tracking script</li>
          </ul>

          <.link
            :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
            navigate={~p"/signup"}
            class="btn btn-primary btn-lg price-action"
          >
            Start free, upgrade later
          </.link>
          <.link
            :if={assigns[:current_user]}
            navigate={~p"/sites"}
            class="btn btn-primary btn-lg price-action"
          >
            Choose a site to upgrade
          </.link>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="home-note">
        Masthead is open source. You can always
        <a href="https://github.com/dijkstrasoftware/masthead" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          run it yourself
        </a>
        instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="pricing-faq-title">
    <div class="home-wrap home-faq">
      <h2 id="pricing-faq-title">Questions about billing</h2>
      <div>
        <details>
          <summary>Is the free plan really free?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. A free site has no expiry date and no card on file. It keeps working
            indefinitely on its masthead.site address.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I pay per account or per site?</summary>
          <p>
            Per site. You can run several sites from one account and license only the
            ones that need a custom domain, collaborators or statistics.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What happens if I cancel?</summary>
          <p>
            The site stays licensed until the period you already paid for runs out, then
            returns to the free plan. Your content is untouched.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I change or cancel my plan?</summary>
          <p>
            From the site's Settings page, under License. That opens the billing portal
            where you can switch plans, update your card, or cancel.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-cta">
    <div class="home-wrap">
      <h2>Start publishing.</h2>
      <p>Create a site for free and upgrade only when you need your own domain.</p>
      <div class="home-actions">
        <.link
          :if={assigns[:current_user]}
          navigate={~p"/sites"}
          class="btn btn-lg home-cta-primary"
        >
          Open dashboard
        </.link>
        <.link
          :if={is_nil(assigns[:current_user])}
          navigate={~p"/signup"}
          class="btn btn-lg home-cta-primary"
        >
          Create your site
        </.link>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />
</div>
